00:17:21,341 --> 00:17:24,509
         I feel like I'm nestled
     in the womb of a Nerf lady.

432
00:17:24,511 --> 00:17:26,511
           Oh, yeah,
      pretty warm, right?

433
00:17:26,513 --> 00:17:28,746
Now how about a nice,
cold beer?

434
00:17:29,648 --> 00:17:31,482
Now, hold on there, chief.

435
00:17:31,484 --> 00:17:32,683
Those ain't free.

436
00:17:32,685 --> 00:17:34,652
              I'm sorry. I don't
                 have any money.

437
00:17:34,654 --> 00:17:37,021
Well, that's good,
'cause we only accept these.

438
00:17:37,023 --> 00:17:38,990
Up high!

439
00:17:38,992 --> 00:17:41,325
Now you're talkin',
Geronimo!

440
00:17:41,327 --> 00:17:44,629
Let's sit down and talk trash
about each other's teams.

441
00:17:46,165 --> 00:17:49,200
          Marvin, 911!
  We just ran out of propane!

442
00:17:49,202 --> 00:17:52,570
Shoot, we'll never get the grill
     up to 400 degrees now!

443
00:17:52,572 --> 00:17:56,841
Ain't no tailgate without
properly seared turkey burgers.

444
00:17:56,843 --> 00:17:59,343
Okay, everyone, pack it up.

445
00:17:59,345 --> 00:18:01,412
We're drivin' back to Texas.

446
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:04,015
                   Wait! Did you
                say 400 degrees?

447
00:18:04,017 --> 00:18:09,754
        Marvin, Laura, it's time
     for <i>me</i> to give back to <i>you.</i>

448
00:18:09,756 --> 00:18:11,255
        (engine revving,
       burgers sizzling)

449
00:18:11,257 --> 00:18:14,592
                Three minutes in
          neutral at 5,000 RPMs!

450
00:18:14,594 --> 00:18:17,195
          That engine block's at
          precisely 400 degrees.

451
00:18:17,197 --> 00:18:18,396
(whoops)
            Yay!

452
00:18:18,398 --> 00:18:20,598
Yee-haw!

453
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:25,736
                  I think you're
                an amazing girl,

454
00:18:25,738 --> 00:18:28,873
           but I'm just not sure
             this is gonna work.

455
00:18:28,875 --> 00:18:30,041
            (crying)

456
00:18:30,043 --> 00:18:33,377
     Not even with youthful
          holiday wig?

457
00:18:33,379 --> 00:18:36,881
         I would say <i>especially </i>
      <i>with youthful holiday wig.</i>

458
00:18:36,883 --> 00:18:38,549
Come on, Mah Mah.

459
00:18:38,551 --> 00:18:40,118
Everyone's waiting
to eat dessert

460
00:18:40,120 --> 00:18:41,886
and is very embarrassed
for you.

461
00:18:41,888 --> 00:18:44,122
        (crying)

462
00:18:45,557 --> 00:18:46,924
Sorry about that.

463
00:18:46,926 --> 00:18:49,894
You want to come downstairs
and have some pie?

464
00:18:49,896 --> 00:18:52,930
Or stay up here and do the same?

465
00:18:52,932 --> 00:18:57,568
         Sorry, Hayley.
 I've made <i>other</i> dessert plans.

466
00:18:57,570 --> 00:18:59,237
    Hayley, you didn't think

467
00:18:59,239 --> 00:19:02,106
 I was gonna let Big Wang slip
  through my fingers, did you?

468
00:19:02,108 --> 00:19:04,442
    Come on, I've still got
   two big installs tonight,

469
00:19:04,444 --> 00:19:07,778
  but only one more job to do,
      if you get my drift.

470
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:10,148
                 (humming)

471
00:19:15,754 --> 00:19:18,756
         Marvin, Laura,
      various other hicks,

472
00:19:18,758 --> 00:19:22,760
 that was the best Thanksgiving
     dinner I've ever had.

473
00:19:22,762 --> 00:19:24,762
Who is this guy?!

474
00:19:24,764 --> 00:19:27,431
       Exactly! Who am I?

475
00:19:27,433 --> 00:19:29,133
        Who am I to you?

476
00:19:29,135 --> 00:19:32,103
      Me, a Redskins fan,
     you, all Cowboy fans.

477
00:19:32,105 --> 00:19:35,439
                      (whooping)

478
00:19:35,441 --> 00:19:37,441
(whooping)
Anyone seen my kid?

479
00:19:37,443 --> 00:19:38,776
(whooping)

480
00:19:38,778 --> 00:19:41,345
  We couldn't be more opposite
          on this day.

481
00:19:41,347 --> 00:19:43,681
      But you welcomed me
    into your parking space

482
00:19:43,683 --> 00:19:45,149
 and taught me how to survive.

483
00:19:45,151 --> 00:19:46,484
                      'Course we
                      did, Stan.

484
00:19:46,486 --> 00:19:47,985
                    'Cause where
                   we come from,

485
00:19:47,987 --> 00:19:50,288
            Thanksgiving's about
       sharing diverse cultures,

486
00:19:50,290 --> 00:19:53,758
        no matter who you are or
       how much your team sucks.

487
00:19:54,626 --> 00:19:56,661
    Or how Chinese you are!

488
00:19:56,663 --> 00:19:58,796
(whooping)

489
00:19:58,798 --> 00:20:01,966
Seriously, I'm gonna be in real
trouble if I can't find him.

490
00:20:01,968 --> 00:20:03,534
(whooping)

491
00:20:06,305 --> 00:20:09,473
           I'm home!
        I made it home!

492
00:20:09,475 --> 00:20:11,309
  Stan, where have you been?!

493
00:20:11,311 --> 00:20:13,678
     You took the trash out
           hours ago!

494
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,513
I've been to a wonderful place.

495
00:20:15,515 --> 00:20:18,349
I was tailgating in the parking
     lot with Cowboys fans.

496
00:20:18,351 --> 00:20:20,985
   They taught me how to make
  a vest out of foam fingers,

497
00:20:20,987 --> 00:20:23,821
       and I taught them
 how to cook burgers on my car.

498
00:20:23,823 --> 00:20:25,990
 And I learned the true meaning
        of Thanksgiving.

499
00:20:25,992 --> 00:20:27,858
That you should accept everyone,

500
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:31,195
  no matter their team colors
   or their skin color or...

501
00:20:31,197 --> 00:20:32,663
   or how horrible they are.

502
00:20:32,665 --> 00:20:35,666
        Oh, that's
        sweet, Stan.

503
00:20:35,668 --> 00:20:38,703
Wait. Why would there be Cowboys
   fans at the Redskins game?

504
00:20:38,705 --> 00:20:41,906
    The Cowboys always play
   in Dallas on Thanksgiving.

505
00:20:41,908 --> 00:20:44,508
             What?
They're gonna ask at Comic-Con.

506
00:20:44,510 --> 00:20:46,344
   We better have an answer!

507
00:20:46,346 --> 00:20:48,813
          Captioned by
   <font color="#00ffff"> Media Access Group at WGBH </font>
        <font color="#00ffff">access.wgbh.org</font>

508
00:21:21,213 --> 00:21:23,347
  Bye! Have a beautiful time.

